{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1551637677,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE5MTM0Mzg4NQ=="},"target":"6c1618203b3a88de99ea4bacd1f4cc72238d01e219060c0a0cfa563c505fb830","message":"ATM this is a leaf command, but I envision it to become more heavily used with the introduction of `--since` type arguments to commands that can perform incremental processing.\n\nThere is a `diff` in -core, but this command is a joke. It doesn't even use properly managed calls to git commands. Key difference between `rev-diff` and `diff` is that the former yields a data structure that is highly similar to that produced by `rev-status` (which should aid adding `--since` to commands that already use `rev-status` internally). Moreover, instead of calling `git diff` it used the same underlying code as `rev-status` and determines differences based on pretty fast `ls-files/ls-tree` calls.\n\nGiven the limited use of `diff` in -core, and its sorry state, I think it is worth considering a hard replacement:\n\n- Expose `rev-diff` as `diff` immediately\n- RF internal usage by `publish`, `annotate-paths`, `rerun` to either use a then purely internal version of the old `diff`, or the new `diff` right away.\n\nThis issue has a relatively low priority. `rev-diff` is likely the least tested of the key -revolution commands, and it is least clear whether its current behavior is optimal wrt all potentially relevant applications.\n\nCheck status of https://github.com/datalad/datalad/pull/3193 for placement in -core.","files":null},{"type":6,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1551637758,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDE1OlVzZXJDb250ZW50RWRpdDE5MTM0NDA0Mg=="},"target":"6c1618203b3a88de99ea4bacd1f4cc72238d01e219060c0a0cfa563c505fb830","message":"ATM this is a leaf command, but I envision it to become more heavily used with the introduction of `--since` type arguments to commands that can perform incremental processing.\n\nThere is a `diff` in -core, but this command is a joke. It doesn't even use properly managed calls to git commands. Key difference between `rev-diff` and `diff` is that the former yields a data structure that is highly similar to that produced by `rev-status` (which should aid adding `--since` to commands that already use `rev-status` internally). Moreover, instead of calling `git diff` it used the same underlying code as `rev-status` and determines differences based on pretty fast `ls-files/ls-tree` calls.\n\nGiven the limited use of `diff` in -core, and its sorry state, I think it is worth considering a hard replacement:\n\n- Expose `rev-diff` as `diff` immediately\n- RF internal usage by `publish`, `annotate-paths`, `rerun` to either use a then purely internal version of the old `diff`, or the new `diff` right away.\n\nThis issue has a relatively low priority. `rev-diff` is likely the least tested of the key -revolution commands, and it is least clear whether its current behavior is optimal wrt all potentially relevant applications.\n\nCheck status of https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3192 for placement in -core.","files":null},{"type":5,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1551512996,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOkxhYmVsZWRFdmVudDIxNzU2NDQ1NDc="},"added":["I-wish-revolution-was-here"],"removed":[]},{"type":3,"author":{"id":"cf7a0bdf96b5195bf3052274368f463c7410f7a8"},"timestamp":1555528790,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDEyOklzc3VlQ29tbWVudDQ4NDIyNTg4Mg==","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/3190#issuecomment-484225882"},"message":"FTR: the metadata command stack rewrite is done and `rev_diff()` did not have to change. I feel confident enough to have it replace -core `diff` -- or be added as `rev_diff()`, if the buggy original needs to stay.","files":null},{"type":4,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1556831839,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDExOkN